    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="IRS990ScheduleO" softwareId="23017517" softwareVersionNum="2023v6.0">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part III, Line 4d</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>OTHER PROGRAM SERVICES 4: SALES - ASSESSMENT MATERIALS OTHER PROGRAM SERVICES 5: PROGRAM DEVELOPMENT:PROGRAM DEVELOPMENT INVOLVED ENHANCEMENTS TO TOPSPRO SOFTWARE, E-TESTS AND CONTINUING DEVELOPMENT OF NEDP. IT ALSO INVOLVED THE DEVELOPMENT OF NEW ASSESSMENTS AND THE RE-VALIDATION OF EXISTING ASSESSMENTS FOR SUBMISSION TO OCTAE FOR APPROVAL.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section A, Line 8b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION HAS A NOMINATING COMMITTEE, AUDIT COMMITTEE, AND FINANCE COMMITTEE. THE COMMITTEES FOLLOW AN AGENDA, BUT THERE IS NO DOCUMENTATION UNTIL BROUGHT TO A FULL BOARD MEETING.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>CONTROLLER PREPARES 990 TAX REQUEST SCHEDULES FOR TAX PREPARER, WHICH IS REVIEWED AND APPROVED BY THE CEO AND CFO. TAX PREPARER SENDS 990 DRAFT TO CONTROLLER. THEN CONTROLLER REVIEWS THE 990 DRAFT WITH THE CEO AND CFO, WHOM APPROVE THE DRAFT. IF CORRECTIONS ARE TO BE MADE, THE DRAFT IS SENT BACK TO THE TAX PREPARER FOR CORRECTIONS. IF NO CORRECTIONS ARE TO BE MADE, A 990 DRAFT IS SENT TO THE CHAIRMAN OF THE BOARD, AUDIT COMMITTEE FOR THE FINAL REVIEW AND APPROVAL. ONCE THE AUDIT CHAIR HAS APPROVED THE 990 FORM, A COPY IS GIVEN TO THE REMAINING BOARD OF DIRECTORS. THEN, CONTROLLER NOTIFIES TAX PREPARER TO PREPARE FINAL 990. CEO OR CFO SIGNS THE FINAL 990 FORM FOR THE IRS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>CASAS HAS A CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY THAT EACH BOARD MEMBER SIGNS ANNUALLY TO ENFORCE COMPLIANCE WITH THE POLICY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>EXECUTIVE AND KEY STAFF COMPENSATION IS DETERMINED BY BENCH MARKING COMPENSATION OF LIKE POSITIONS WITH THE CALIFORNIA DEPARTMENT OF EDUCATION, THE SACRAMENTO COUNTY OFFICE OF EDUCATION, THE SAN DIEGO COMMUNITY COLLEGE DISTRICT, 990'S OF COMPARABLE ORGANIZATION, AND THE ECONOMIC RESEARCH INSTITUTE-NONPROFIT COMPARABLE ASSESSOR. EXECUTIVE COMPENSATION IS APPROVED BY THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, Line 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION MAKES ITS GOVERNING DOCUMENTS, CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY AND FINANCIAL STATEMENTS AVAILABLE UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
